{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {"id": "title"},
      "source": [
        "# Outcome-aware SPP-assisted LSTM Cache Action Predictor\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook is the Colab / cluster orchestration notebook for the project diagram.\n",
        "\n",
        "Main idea:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "SPP is candidate + context + supervision.\n",
        "LSTM is the cache-action learner.\n",
        "The goal is not only next-address prediction.\n",
        "The goal is useful / non-duplicate prefetch + bypass / priority + timing.\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "The actual trainer used by this notebook is:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "formal_NN_training/scripts/train_lstm_cache_action.py\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "That script keeps the model code out of the notebook so Colab and cluster run the exact same training logic.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {"id": "workflow"},
      "source": [
        "## Workflow\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "cluster: ChampSim + instrumented SPP -> lstm_events_<TRACE>.csv\n",
        "Colab/cluster: this notebook -> train_lstm_cache_action.py -> action CSV\n",
        "cluster: action CSV -> prefetch list -> ChampSim replay\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Default first trace: `602.gcc_s-734B` because it is mixed / phase behavior and is the most general first pipeline test.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {"id": "config"},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# 0. Config\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import os, json, subprocess, textwrap, gzip, shutil\n",
        "\n",
        "TRACE = os.environ.get('TRACE', '602.gcc_s-734B')\n",
        "REPO_NAME = 'cache_arch'\n",
        "GITHUB_USERNAME = 'Angelawoo572'\n",
        "REPO_ROOT = Path('/content') / REPO_NAME if Path('/content').exists() else Path.cwd()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Training knobs. Start with smoke, then set RUN_MAIN=True.\n",
        "RUN_SMOKE = True\n",
        "RUN_MAIN = False\n",
        "SMOKE_MAX_ROWS = 500_000\n",
        "MAIN_MAX_ROWS = 2_000_000   # use 0 for full CSV\n",
        "\n",
        "SEQ_LEN_SMOKE = 32\n",
        "SEQ_LEN_MAIN = 64\n",
        "GOOD_THRESHOLD = 0.50\n",
        "BYPASS_THRESHOLD = 0.60\n",
        "\n",
        "print('TRACE =', TRACE)\n",
        "print('REPO_ROOT =', REPO_ROOT)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {"id": "pull-md"},
      "source": [
        "## 1. GitHub pull / clone\n",
        "\n",
        "Use this in Colab. It clones or hard-resets to `origin/main`. The remote is set back to the safe URL after pulling so the PAT is not left in `git remote -v`.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {"id": "pull"},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from getpass import getpass\n",
        "\n",
        "token = os.environ.get('GITHUB_PAT')\n",
        "if token is None and not REPO_ROOT.exists():\n",
        "    token = getpass('GitHub PAT for clone/pull: ')\n",
        "    os.environ['GITHUB_PAT'] = token\n",
        "\n",
        "safe_url = f'https://github.com/{GITHUB_USERNAME}/{REPO_NAME}.git'\n",
        "if not REPO_ROOT.exists():\n",
        "    auth_url = f'https://{GITHUB_USERNAME}:{token}@github.com/{GITHUB_USERNAME}/{REPO_NAME}.git'\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['git', 'clone', auth_url, str(REPO_ROOT)], check=True)\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)\n",
        "    if token:\n",
        "        auth_url = f'https://{GITHUB_USERNAME}:{token}@github.com/{GITHUB_USERNAME}/{REPO_NAME}.git'\n",
        "        subprocess.run(['git', 'remote', 'set-url', 'origin', auth_url], check=True)\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['git', 'fetch', 'origin', 'main'], check=True)\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['git', 'reset', '--hard', 'origin/main'], check=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)\n",
        "subprocess.run(['git', 'remote', 'set-url', 'origin', safe_url], check=True)\n",
        "subprocess.run(['git', 'log', '--oneline', '-5'], check=True)\n",
        "subprocess.run(['git', 'status', '--short'], check=True)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {"id": "restore-md"},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Restore split / compressed input data in Colab\n",
        "\n",
        "Expected upload layout:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "formal_NN_training/data/upload/602/lstm_events_602.gcc_s-734B.csv.gz.part_000 ...\n",
        "formal_NN_training/data/upload/602/candidate_table_602.gcc_s-734B.csv.gz.part_000 ... optional\n",
        "formal_NN_training/data/upload/602/spp_events_602.gcc_s-734B.csv.gz.part_000 ... optional\n",
        "```\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {"id": "restore"},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)\n",
        "restore_script = Path('formal_NN_training/scripts/00_restore_colab_uploaded_data.sh')\n",
        "events_csv = Path(f'formal_NN_training/data/generated/lstm_events_{TRACE}.csv')\n",
        "\n",
        "if events_csv.exists():\n",
        "    print('[reuse]', events_csv, events_csv.stat().st_size)\n",
        "elif restore_script.exists():\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['bash', str(restore_script)], check=True, env={**os.environ, 'TRACE': TRACE})\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    raise FileNotFoundError('No events CSV and no restore script found.')\n",
        "\n",
        "subprocess.run(['ls', '-lh', str(events_csv)], check=True)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {"id": "schema-md"},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Sanity-check event table\n",
        "\n",
        "The outcome-aware trainer requires `outcome_useful` and `outcome_duplicate`. If these are missing, the SPP dump step was not the right instrumented dump.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {"id": "schema"},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "sample = pd.read_csv(events_csv, nrows=200_000)\n",
        "print('columns:', list(sample.columns))\n",
        "for c in ['hit', 'spp_issued', 'outcome_useful', 'outcome_duplicate', 'pf_addr', 'delta', 'spp_confidence']:\n",
        "    if c in sample.columns:\n",
        "        print('\\n', c)\n",
        "        print(sample[c].value_counts(dropna=False).head(10))\n",
        "        try:\n",
        "            print('mean =', pd.to_numeric(sample[c], errors='coerce').mean())\n",
        "        except Exception:\n",
        "            pass\n",
        "required = {'pc', 'addr', 'outcome_useful', 'outcome_duplicate'}\n",
        "missing = required - set(sample.columns)\n",
        "if missing:\n",
        "    raise ValueError(f'Missing required columns: {missing}')\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {"id": "train-md"},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Train outcome-aware LSTM in Colab\n",
        "\n",
        "This is still Colab training. The notebook calls the shared Python trainer so cluster and Colab use the same code.\n",
        "\n",
        "Primary labels:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "good_prefetch = outcome_useful == 1 AND outcome_duplicate == 0\n",
        "bypass / low-priority = duplicate OR useless OR self-candidate\n",
        "timing = future distance bucket for candidate line\n",
        "```\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {"id": "train-smoke"},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)\n",
        "if RUN_SMOKE:\n",
        "    cmd = [\n",
        "        'python3', 'formal_NN_training/scripts/train_lstm_cache_action.py',\n",
        "        '--trace', TRACE,\n",
        "        '--events', str(events_csv),\n",
        "        '--max-rows', str(SMOKE_MAX_ROWS),\n",
        "        '--seq-len', str(SEQ_LEN_SMOKE),\n",
        "        '--epochs', '2',\n",
        "        '--batch-size', '128',\n",
        "        '--hidden-dim', '96',\n",
        "        '--emb-dim', '32',\n",
        "        '--good-threshold', str(GOOD_THRESHOLD),\n",
        "        '--bypass-threshold', str(BYPASS_THRESHOLD),\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "    print(' '.join(cmd))\n",
        "    subprocess.run(cmd, check=True)\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print('[skip] RUN_SMOKE=False')\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {"id": "train-main"},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)\n",
        "if RUN_MAIN:\n",
        "    cmd = [\n",
        "        'python3', 'formal_NN_training/scripts/train_lstm_cache_action.py',\n",
        "        '--trace', TRACE,\n",
        "        '--events', str(events_csv),\n",
        "        '--max-rows', str(MAIN_MAX_ROWS),\n",
        "        '--seq-len', str(SEQ_LEN_MAIN),\n",
        "        '--epochs', '8',\n",
        "        '--batch-size', '256',\n",
        "        '--hidden-dim', '128',\n",
        "        '--emb-dim', '32',\n",
        "        '--good-threshold', str(GOOD_THRESHOLD),\n",
        "        '--bypass-threshold', str(BYPASS_THRESHOLD),\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "    print(' '.join(cmd))\n",
        "    subprocess.run(cmd, check=True)\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print('[skip] RUN_MAIN=False. Set RUN_MAIN=True after smoke test passes.')\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {"id": "summary-md"},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Read training summary\n",
        "\n",
        "Read these first: `good_precision`, `good_recall`, `good_f1`, `emit_precision_good`, `emit_duplicate_rate`.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {"id": "summary"},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "summary_path = Path('formal_NN_training/artifacts/outcome_lstm_summary.json')\n",
        "history_path = Path('formal_NN_training/artifacts/outcome_lstm_training_history.csv')\n",
        "if summary_path.exists():\n",
        "    summary = json.loads(summary_path.read_text())\n",
        "    print(json.dumps(summary.get('label_meta', {}), indent=2))\n",
        "    print(json.dumps(summary.get('final_val_metrics', {}), indent=2))\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print('[missing]', summary_path)\n",
        "if history_path.exists():\n",
        "    display(pd.read_csv(history_path).tail())\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {"id": "convert-md"},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Convert action CSV to list_replayer prefetch list\n",
        "\n",
        "This can run in Colab. Actual ChampSim replay usually runs on cluster because Colab does not have traces / built ChampSim.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {"id": "convert"},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "actions_csv = Path('formal_NN_training/artifacts/full_lstm_cache_actions.csv')\n",
        "prefetch_list = Path(f'formal_NN_training/results/replay_compare/prefetch_lists/prefetch_list_{TRACE}_outcome_lstm.txt')\n",
        "if actions_csv.exists():\n",
        "    subprocess.run([\n",
        "        'python3', 'formal_NN_training/scripts/02_actions_to_prefetch_list.py',\n",
        "        '--actions', str(actions_csv),\n",
        "        '--out', str(prefetch_list),\n",
        "        '--policy', 'action',\n",
        "        '--prefetch-threshold', str(GOOD_THRESHOLD),\n",
        "        '--bypass-threshold', str(BYPASS_THRESHOLD),\n",
        "    ], check=True)\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['wc', '-l', str(prefetch_list)], check=True)\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['head', str(prefetch_list)], check=False)\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print('[missing]', actions_csv)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {"id": "replay-md"},
      "source": [
        "## 7. Optional cluster replay\n",
        "\n",
        "This cell runs only when `external/ChampSim/bin/champsim.replayer` and the trace file exist. In Colab it normally skips.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {"id": "replay"},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "replayer = Path('external/ChampSim/bin/champsim.replayer')\n",
        "trace_file = Path(f'traces/{TRACE}.champsimtrace.xz')\n",
        "if replayer.exists() and trace_file.exists():\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['bash', 'formal_NN_training/scripts/03_run_lstm_replay.sh'], check=True, env={\n",
        "        **os.environ,\n",
        "        'TRACE': TRACE,\n",
        "        'WARMUP': os.environ.get('WARMUP', '25000000'),\n",
        "        'SIM': os.environ.get('SIM', '25000000'),\n",
        "        'POLICY': 'action',\n",
        "        'PREFETCH_THRESHOLD': str(GOOD_THRESHOLD),\n",
        "        'BYPASS_THRESHOLD': str(BYPASS_THRESHOLD),\n",
        "    })\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print('[skip] No ChampSim replayer / trace here. Train in Colab, replay on cluster.')\n",
        "    print('Cluster command:')\n",
        "    print(f'TRACE={TRACE} WARMUP=25000000 SIM=25000000 POLICY=action PREFETCH_THRESHOLD={GOOD_THRESHOLD} BYPASS_THRESHOLD={BYPASS_THRESHOLD} bash formal_NN_training/scripts/03_run_lstm_replay.sh')\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {"id": "pack-md"},
      "source": [
        "## 8. Pack / split large outputs\n",
        "\n",
        "GitHub should track code, notebook, README, and small summaries. Large CSV / `.pt` files should be compressed and split instead of committed directly.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {"id": "pack"},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "PACK_DIR = Path(f'formal_NN_training/artifacts/packed/{TRACE.split(".")[0]}')\n",
        "PACK_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "def gzip_file(src: Path, dst: Path):\n",
        "    if not src.exists():\n",
        "        print('[skip missing]', src)\n",
        "        return\n",
        "    with src.open('rb') as f_in, gzip.open(dst, 'wb') as f_out:\n",
        "        shutil.copyfileobj(f_in, f_out)\n",
        "    print('[gzip]', src, '->', dst, dst.stat().st_size)\n",
        "\n",
        "gz_actions = PACK_DIR / 'full_lstm_cache_actions.csv.gz'\n",
        "gzip_file(Path('formal_NN_training/artifacts/full_lstm_cache_actions.csv'), gz_actions)\n",
        "\n",
        "if gz_actions.exists():\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['bash', '-lc', f'rm -f {gz_actions}.part_* && split -b 90m {gz_actions} {gz_actions}.part_ && ls -lh {PACK_DIR}'], check=True)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {"id": "push-md"},
      "source": [
        "## 9. Optional GitHub push\n",
        "\n",
        "This stages source files only. Do not force-add huge generated CSV / model files.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {"id": "push"},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "DO_GIT_PUSH = False\n",
        "if DO_GIT_PUSH:\n",
        "    token = os.environ.get('GITHUB_PAT') or getpass('GitHub PAT for push: ')\n",
        "    auth_url = f'https://{GITHUB_USERNAME}:{token}@github.com/{GITHUB_USERNAME}/{REPO_NAME}.git'\n",
        "    safe_url = f'https://github.com/{GITHUB_USERNAME}/{REPO_NAME}.git'\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['git', 'config', 'user.name', 'Angela Wu'], check=True)\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['git', 'config', 'user.email', 'Angelawoo572@users.noreply.github.com'], check=True)\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['git', 'add',\n",
        "                    'formal_NN_training/LSTM_cache_action_predictor.ipynb',\n",
        "                    'formal_NN_training/scripts/train_lstm_cache_action.py',\n",
        "                    'formal_NN_training/scripts/02_actions_to_prefetch_list.py',\n",
        "                    'formal_NN_training/README_LSTM_cache_action_predictor.md'], check=True)\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['git', 'status', '--short'], check=True)\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['git', 'commit', '-m', 'Run outcome-aware LSTM cache action workflow'], check=False)\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['git', 'remote', 'set-url', 'origin', auth_url], check=True)\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['git', 'push', 'origin', 'main'], check=True)\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['git', 'remote', 'set-url', 'origin', safe_url], check=True)\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    subprocess.run(['git', 'status', '--short'], check=True)\n"
      ]
    }
  ],
